!! Module overview

|!Module |!Type |!Purpose |
|`startup.js` |startup |Registers the three hooks (`after: load-modules`, `before: frontmatter`) |
|`hooks.js` |library |Hook implementations: scope decision, config, file paths |
|`mapping.js` |library |OKF document ↔ tiddler fields (`fromOkf`, `toOkf`, `load`, `dump`) |
|`scope.js` |library |`isTwType`, `isOkfType`, `matchesFilter` |
|`js-yaml.js` |library |Bundled js-yaml 4.1.0 (MIT) |

!! Load

```
.md ─► frontmatter document.parse ─► th-frontmatter-parse ─► okf onParse
         js-yaml (FAILSAFE) ─► fromOkf ─► in scope? ─► replace the flat fields
```

* The flat-parse keys (`info.parsed`) and `type` are removed, the mapped fields added; fields preset by the caller stay
* Out of scope or invalid YAML: the flat frontmatter result is returned unchanged (invalid YAML is logged)
* `info.pathTitle` supplies the title when the YAML names none (`tw.title` or, for frontmatter files, `title`)

!! Save

```
tiddler ─► generateTiddlerFileInfo ─► th-frontmatter-fileinfo ─► okf onFileInfo (path)
        ─► document.build ─► th-frontmatter-serialize ─► okf onSerialize ─► toOkf ─► js-yaml dump
```

* Scope on save: `okf.type` set (and not a TW type) ''or'' the filter matches
* `tw.title` is written when `title` ≠ the title the file path yields (`info.pathTitle`)
* File path: the existing `.md` of the tiddler if there is one, else `generateTiddlerFilepath` with a pass-through path filter — `/` become folders, invalid characters are replaced by core

!! Why the FAILSAFE schema

js-yaml's FAILSAFE schema reads every scalar as a string and writes strings without type quoting. TW dates (17 digits, beyond JS number precision) stay exact, and `usage_count: 5000` is written back as `5000`, not `"5000"`.

